    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 59 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe registration-date business-day rule now extends to public holidays. I updated the single production class responsible for the roll:\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDay.java`**\n\n- Added the fixed public-holiday list: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Changed `roll(...)` from a single weekend hop to a loop that advances one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed holiday \u2014 so it lands on the next non-holiday business day.\n\nThis correctly handles cascades (e.g. `2026-12-25` is a Friday holiday \u2192 skip Sat/Sun 26\u201327 \u2192 `2026-12-28` is also a holiday \u2192 land on `2026-12-29`), which the prior fixed `plusDays` logic could not.\n\nThe caller (`ResolveRegistrationDate`) and the `RejectFutureRegistrationDate` guard needed no changes. The full suite (59 tests, including `Cp47Tests` for holiday-business-day and the `Cp19`/`Cp20` tests that compare against the test-side `toBusinessDay` helper) passes.",
